It's a fun and short game, I would recommend it to those who want to kill an hour or so.
Pros:
- looks nice;
- has okay music;
- easy to control (with mouse);
- I was quite pleasantly surprised by enemy placement, some are hard to predict which side of the screen they would appear;
- Megaman-like challenge introduction. I mean, the first time you see a new challenge it is almost impossible to die from it.
Cons:
- boring. Only 3 powerups, one of which is rudimentary, and only one is upgradeable;
- It's a BULLET-HELL, or at least a bullet-storm (cause its easy). No-one said that. I hate bullet-hells. Here I thought I was gonna play an old school shmup, swishing and swooshing across the screen like a sofa ace. Heck no. Shame;
- kinda continues the previous. Too many unnecessary debris, enemy projectiles are sometimes the same color as yours. Since it's a bullet-something, it makes it unjustly harder.
- special weapon is not a "let me catch my breath for a moment" since it doesn't destroy every enemy bullet on the screen.
There. I wouldn't have written this, but I was really♥♥♥♥♥♥♥♥for it to not have a "bullet-hell" tag.

* Unlocking the next level is mostly based on chance and not on skills;
* Bad electro music;
* Over-priced, should be free.

